L000173	The scattering coefficient matrix can be obtained via Fourier transformation and the input–output relation~\cite{PhysRevA.31.3761,PhysRevA.85.021801}~(see the Supplemental Material~\cite{Supplement}, Sec. VI). The transmission coefficient from mode $b$ to mode $a$ vanishes, $T_{ab}=0$, whereas from mode $a$ to mode $b$ is denoted by $T_{ba}$, which reaches its maximum when the squeezed-cavity frequency is zero, as shown in Fig.~\ref{fig3}(a). When $\omega_s=0$, $T_{ba}$ is given by
